   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": null,
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Suppose that the rewards distributions belong to a $1$-dimensional canonical exponential family and that $\\pi_J$ is the Jeffrey's prior. Then, \\lim_{T\\ra \\infty} \\frac {\\cR(\\phi^{TS,\\pi_J},T)}{\\ln T} = \\sum_{a = 1}^K \\frac{\\mu(\\theta_{a^*})-\\mu(\\theta_a)}{\\K(\\theta_a, \\theta_{a^*})}"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Stated as an equality of the limit (matching the Lai-Robbins lower bound); recorded as limsup upper bound. Follows from Theorem 2. Regret defined via means, so pseudo-regret."
  },
  {
   "id": "r2",
