    "any eps_alg > 0 (analysis parameter)"
   ],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:main",
    "number": "Theorem 2",
    "quote": "Assume that $\\mu_1>\\mu_a$ for all $a\\neq 1$, and that $\\pi_{a,0}$ is taken to be the Jeffrey's prior over $\\Theta$. Then for every $\\epsilon>0$ there exists a constant $\\cC(\\epsilon,\\cP)$ depending on $\\epsilon$ and on the problem $\\mathcal{P}$ such that the regret of Thompson Sampling using the Jeffrey's prior satisfies \\cR(\\phi^{TS,\\pi_J},T) \\leq \\frac{1+\\epsilon}{1-\\epsilon}\\left(\\sum_{a=2}^{K}\\frac{(\\mu_1-\\mu_a)}{\\K(\\theta_a,\\theta_1)}\\right)\\ln(T) + \\mathcal{C}(\\epsilon,\\mathcal{P})."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "KL_i = K(theta_a, theta_1) = KL(p_a, p_1). Constant is non-explicit (relies on Bernstein-von Mises argument)."
  }
